OSMesa takes the GPU, makes OpenGL ES contexts, and imports IOSurfaces as EGL images.

- GL/osmesa.h, frontends/osmesa/osmesa.c: OSMESA_ES_PROFILE (0x38) makes an OpenGL ES 2/3 context (HakiOS osmesa-es-profile.patch).
- frontends/osmesa/osmesa.c: get_egl_image/validate_egl_image: the "EGLImage" of glEGLImageTargetTexture2DOES is an IOSurface ID
  (HakiOS freedreno-darwin.patch), resolved by osmesa_surface_resource().
- targets/osmesa/osmesa_target.c: the screen is gallium panfrost on drm_darwin_open_render()'s descriptor when MaliService exists
  (softpipe otherwise, or with OSMESA_SOFTWARE=1; OSMESA_DEBUG_GPU=1 prints why the GPU was not taken). osmesa_surface_resource()
  makes a linear B8G8R8A8 resource of a 'BGRA', single-plane IOSurface (resource_from_handle with the ID as the "fd").
  Unlike the S9 (hakios-drm, panfrost kmod, its kernel's own surface request) this goes through darwin-drm and panthor.

